{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791382819,"nonce":"0IXMXkwKXJ8Q652JwdQtepqGnqg=","title":"Forward class members and inherited generic callbacks lose their declared types","message":"Related cluster: 3ac7905f1b1764c8a41bc19a9014b6b1c2d595bd68ff2869dca9e7099794333e. This issue covers forward data-field identity, early class parameter/superclass registration, constructor callback typing, and specialization of callback parameters in generated closures. Other missing-method cases remain in the parent issue.\n\nRepro: haxe-conformance/regressions/ForwardClassMembers.hx. A main class preceding LaterBox\u003cT\u003e and LaterSignal\u003cT\u003e reads/writes Float fields and properties, constructs LaterSignal\u003cFloat\u003e with an unannotated capturing callback, calls an inherited callback field, and reads that field as a function value. Int and contextually inferred String instances exercise separate constructor instantiations. Native Haxe accepts the fixture and prints CONFORMANCE_OK.\n\nBefore the change the fixture traps at an uncompiled LaterSignal.callback placeholder. Issue7334 similarly traps at an uncompiled Signal1.dispatch. Class field pre-registration lacked class parameter and superclass bindings, and full class lowering replaced the pre-registered field list, changing field identities used by earlier declarations. Constructor arguments were lowered before contextual callback types were available.\n\nMIR evidence: the forwarder originally accepted an erased i64 parameter while its Float caller used an f64 parameter. The actual handler was inferred Dynamic, which makes the Int corpus case dereference the raw value as a box. Carrying constructor parameter hints fixes the handler; generated callback parameter types and indirect signatures must also specialize with the enclosing generic body. Variable reads must preserve those type variables until specialization rather than numerically cast them to erased i64.\n\nRejected candidate v3 specialized captured values as well as callback parameters. It scored 873/1094 against the verified 885/1094 baseline, losing twelve passing rows, and failed AbstractGenericFrom's Float assertion. Captured scalar storage and erased closure returns must retain their existing conventions. Candidate v4 restored those passing thread tests but still numerically cast the forwarder's Float parameter to i64. Candidate v5 passes the new fixture and Issue7334 but changes Issue4578 from PASS to WRONG_ANSWER: supplying unbound constructor parameters as callback hints prevents inference from the body and changes an integer callback result to Float. Constructor class parameters without concrete arguments must be inferred from arguments.\n\nValidation logs and reports: /tmp/rayzor-forward-members-*. Final checkpoint results will be recorded before closing.","files":null}]}